<decision #upgrade-depa-data-graph-package-baseline.scope apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV5>
  Should package resolution and source migration be implemented in the same track？
  </?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV5>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV6>
    No.
    </?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV6>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV7>
    This track upgrades direct manifests and bun.lock, then updates only the boundary guard. Source-level unified API migration stays in the successor tracks.
    </?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV7>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV8>
    The upstream release is breaking and the mission needs an observable dependency baseline before distinct behavior owners change their graph code.
    </?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV8>
    <evidence ?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV9>
    The containing mission G1 baseline reports and target migration contract.
    </?01M05F1PMH1XJMVWPPFA60BDV9>
  )>
)>
